		<task label="hw-while-collatz">

			<statement>
				<p>
					A famous problem in math is the Collatz conjecture, which states that if you start with any positive integer and repeatedly apply the following rules, you will eventually reach 1:
					<ul>
						<li>If the number is even, divide it by 2.</li>	
						<li>If the number is odd, multiply it by 3 and add 1.</li>
					</ul>
				</p>

				<p>
					For example, starting with 6:
					<md>
						<mrow>6 \to 3 \to 10 \to 5 \to 16 \to 8 \to 4 \to 2 \to 1</mrow>
					</md>
				</p>

				<p>
					Despite its simple statement, the Collatz conjecture has not been proven or disproven, and it remains an open question in mathematics. In this exercise, you will write a MATLAB script to explore the Collatz conjecture for different starting values.
				</p>

				<p>
					Write a function called <pf>collatzSteps</pf> that uses a <pf>while</pf> loop to return the number of steps required for the sequence to reach <m>1</m>.
				</p>
				<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
					<col width="11%"/>
					<col width="15%"/>
					<col width="28%" halign="left"/>
					<col width="46%" halign="left"/>
					<row>
						<cell>Difficulty:</cell><cell>★</cell><cell/><cell/>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>Inputs:</cell>
						<cell><p><pf>x</pf></p></cell>
						<cell><p>(1x1) double</p></cell>
						<cell><p>starting number (positive)</p></cell>
					</row>
					<row bottom="minor">
						<cell>Outputs:</cell>
						<cell><p><pf>steps</pf></p></cell>
						<cell><p>(1x1) double</p></cell>
						<cell><p>number of steps to reach 1</p></cell>
					</row>
				</tabular>
				<sidebyside widths="50% 48%">
					<stack>
						<p>Test Cases ⤵︎</p>
						<program language="matlab">
							steps = collatzSteps(6)
							steps = collatzSteps(10)
							steps = collatzSteps(1)
							steps = collatzSteps(27)
						</program>
					</stack>
					<stack>
						<p>Expected ⤵︎</p>
						<program language="matlab">
							% steps = 8
							% steps = 6
							% steps = 0
							% steps = 111
						</program>
					</stack>
				</sidebyside>
			</statement>
		</task>

